Based on the details you provided, your Australian passport expires on July 22, 2029. Because that date is well into the future, your passport is highly likely to be valid for travel right now. 

Here is a checklist to help you verify that your document is fully valid and ready for your visa application and travel:

1. **The 6-Month Rule:** Most countries require your passport to be valid for at least 6 months beyond your planned date of entry or departure from their country. Since your passport expires in 2029, you easily meet this requirement for any near-term travel.
2. **Blank Pages:** Open your passport and check the visa pages. Many countries require you to have at least one to two completely blank pages for entry stamps and the physical visa sticker.
